WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.325
Before the first gate, three things.

2
00:00:02.325 --> 00:00:07.325
Decisions first: who owns each provider's
notices, which notices become tasks,

3
00:00:07.325 --> 00:00:12.637
for which group and at which severity, and
who receives each provider's email today.

4
00:00:12.637 --> 00:00:14.900
That routing belongs to the agency.

5
00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:18.969
It's written at work from the
kit's template, with its prompts in

6
00:00:18.969 --> 00:00:23.437
Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat, and it
never goes in a public repository.

7
00:00:23.437 --> 00:00:26.588
Second, a change process
that takes the tasks.

8
00:00:26.588 --> 00:00:30.646
The router writes ServiceNow-shaped
payloads, and until the agency

9
00:00:30.646 --> 00:00:34.487
builds an endpoint for them, they're
files the service desk reads.

10
00:00:34.487 --> 00:00:38.700
Third, a reader per provider,
holding only its read role.

11
00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:42.812
The roles come from each provider's
own documentation, and they're short.

12
00:00:42.812 --> 00:00:46.872
The writes, meaning the Azure
Policy assignment and rollback,

13
00:00:46.872 --> 00:00:51.310
run as a different identity, and
only with an explicit apply switch.
